{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_erovvokwrnvgdmmw3zid7jslot6xareduhjdzas7jrdwzbhjbdva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What the project is\n\n`c_src/` is a 3-file, preprocessor-driven C project (`mdcore.c`, `mdmain.c`, `mdmacros.h`) configured by two CMake cache variables — `OP` ∈ {`add`,`sub`,`mul`} and `REPEAT` ∈ 0..7 — giving **24 build configurations**, mapped to Cargo features of the same names (plus `repeat_N` aliases and \"unset ⇒ default\" spellings, 60 configurations in all).\n\n## Phase A artifacts (created)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 8 exported symbols from `nm -D`, with C↔Rust name/type/section parity |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 22-row error-surface table, mechanically grepped from the C |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 33-row configuration-surface table over `OP` × `REPEAT` × entry point × input shape |\n| `VERIFICATION.md` | how to reproduce, what diverged, completion gate |\n\n## Real divergences found and fixed (Rust only; `c_src/` untouched)\n\n1. **`G_OP`/`G_OP_NAME` in the wrong ELF section** — Rust put them in `.data.rel.ro` (read-only after RELRO); the C non-`const` globals live in writable `.data`. A C consumer assigning to `G_OP` would have trapped. Fixed with `#[unsafe(link_section = \".data\")]`.\n2. **`print!` panicked on stdout write errors** — with stdout on `/dev/full` the C exited 0, Rust aborted (134). Replaced with an error-dropping `c_printf` in `mdcore.rs` and `main.rs`.\n3. **`argv[0]` ran through `to_string_lossy`** — a non-UTF-8 program path produced U+FFFD (23 bytes vs the C's 19). `usage()` now writes raw bytes.\n4. Cosmetic clippy lints.\n\n## Results (all green)\n\n- `cargo check`: **60/60** feature configurations clean; `cargo clippy --all-targets` clean.\n- Symbol parity: **8/8** symbols, exact name + `nm` type + size, **0** undefined non-libc symbols, in all 24 configurations.\n- Phase B/C: **41 differential tests** (loading *both* `.so`s via `libloading`, comparing return values *and* captured fd-1 bytes) × **60 configurations**, all passing — every `CONFIGS.md` and `ERRORS.md` row checked off (row 18 is `NULL`-function-pointer UB that kills both, documented not executed).\n- **648** C-executable vs Rust-executable comparisons (stdout + stderr + exit status) identical.\n- `--release` (`panic = \"abort\"`) also builds, exports and behaves identically for all 24 configurations.\n- **Anti-vacuity:** `scripts/mutation_check.sh` injects 18 behavioural mutations and all 18 are caught.\n\nOne documented, deliberate deviation remains: `SIGPIPE` disposition (Rust's std sets `SIG_IGN` before `main`), explained at the end of `ERRORS.md` — it is unreachable in any scenario where the two programs' output can actually be compared."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":454,"cache_read_input_tokens":243895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":454,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70a99c7d-b458-4bc3-9410-f85c2d2f8dd4","uuid":"3faa9f16-69df-4a44-949c-9c67274b2de9","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:11:31.912Z"}
